{"kind":"finding","id":"FN-B-run-phone-tracker-services-1-b-01","date":"2026-11-25","lens":"gap-8","surface":"phone","area":"phone/tracker-services-1","refs":["F-phone-536"],"severity":"S4","title":"After a reinstall, a progress photo that fails to come back from the backup stays blank with no word","what":"With 'Include photos in my backup' on, a fresh install puts each progress photo back from the backed-up copy at app start. If copying one photo back fails, the error is swallowed with no message and no log line: that photo stays a blank square, the member is not told it could not be brought back, and nobody can tell why later. The next start tries again, so a passing hiccup heals itself, but a lasting one never surfaces.","expected":"When a backed-up photo cannot be put back, the member is told how many photos could not be restored, and the failure is noted for the team.","evidence":["apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/photoBackup.ts:389-402","apps/mobile/src/tracker/services/photoBackup.ts:413-414","apps/mobile/src/app/_layout.tsx:121"],"proof":"code-read","root_cause_key":"photo-relink-failure-swallowed","who":"members who turned on photos in backup and reinstall","how_often":"rarely (only when a photo copy fails during restore)","fix_line":"Log each failed photo restore and show a short count of photos that could not be brought back.","fix_size":"small","needs_him":false,"verified":"pending","status":"open"}
